        "prompt": "Explore the Twenty monorepo at /Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite to map the NATIVE CSV/bulk import/export pipeline(s) for records (especially tasks). I need a thorough report with exact file paths and key exported functions/symbols.\n\nFind and report:\n1. Frontend import: files under packages/twenty-front related to importing records — e.g. components named Import*, hooks/state (import logic store), CSV parsing, validation of rows, mapping columns to fields, error/partial-row feedback UI (e.g. import preview, \"Import data\" steps, per-row errors). Look for directories like `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/import-record` or `object-record/import`, `spreadsheet-import`, and any `import` feature module. List key entry components, hooks, and the shape of the row-validation types (e.g. ImportedRow, validation errors).\n2. Backend import: packages/twenty-server modules handling import — e.g. `import-job`, `import-record`, CSV parser/validator services, the mutation `uploadImportFile`/`importRecords` GraphQL, entities like ImportJob/ImportJobItem, and any per-row error storage. List key services and their public methods.\n3. Export: native export pipeline — `export-record`, `export-job`, CSV generation utilities in twenty-server/twenty-front, and the GraphQL mutations/queries.\n4. How tasks (standard `task` object) are treated by import — any special-casing, required fields, relation/many-to-many handling (e.g. labels, assignee), and permission checks.\n5. Any existing tests for import validation/escaping/error feedback (paths + what they cover).\n6. The app SDK capabilities available to a Twenty app (packages/twenty-sdk and packages/twenty-apps/internal/real-estate) that relate to import/export or to front components that could call native import — does the SDK expose anything for import? Is there a way for an app front-component to reuse native import UI/store?\n\nBe precise: give file paths, exported symbol names, and short descriptions. Do not modify any files. Report concisely but completely.",
