        "result": "<task id=\"ses_f444f1605ffexHW3gT5uRu8VEg\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n# Native CSV / Bulk Import-Export Pipeline Map — A2E Suite (Twenty monorepo)\n\n## Headline finding\n\nThis checkout has **no server-side CSV import or export pipeline**. There are no `import-job` / `import-record` / `export-job` / `export-record` modules, no `ImportJob` / `ImportJobItem` entities, and no `uploadImportFile` / `importRecords` / `exportRecords` GraphQL mutations anywhere in `packages/twenty-server`. I searched all of `packages/twenty-server/src` and both generated schemas (`packages/twenty-front/src/generated-metadata/graphql.ts`, `packages/twenty-client-sdk/src/metadata/generated/schema.graphql`) — no matches.\n\nInstead:\n- **Import is 100% client-side**: the frontend parses CSV/XLSX, validates rows, maps them to fields, and submits via the standard object-record `createMany` GraphQL mutation (`upsert: true`).\n- **Export is 100% client-side**: the frontend fetches records and generates the CSV in the browser with `json-2-csv`.\n\nThe only \"server-side\" import code is unrelated integrations (calendar/messaging sync) and an app-level import helper in `twenty-apps/public/call-recorder`, not the native record importer.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Frontend import\n\nTwo cooperating modules:\n\n### A. Generic engine — `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/spreadsheet-import/`\nA self-contained spreadsheet-import wizard (adapted from `react-spreadsheet-import`; \"Rsi\" = React Spreadsheet Import).\n\nEntry / provider:\n- `provider/components/SpreadsheetImportProvider.tsx` — `SpreadsheetImportProvider` (React.lazy-loads `SpreadsheetImport`), reads `spreadsheetImportDialogState`, handles close/abort.\n- `provider/components/SpreadsheetImport.tsx` — `SpreadsheetImport`, `defaultSpreadsheetImportProps` (maxRecords, autoMapHeaders, autoMapDistance, dateFormat `yyyy-mm-dd`, parseRaw, `allowInvalidSubmit: true`).\n- `components/ReactSpreadsheetImportContextProvider.tsx` — `ReactSpreadsheetImportContextProvider`, `RsiContext`.\n- `hooks/useSpreadsheetImportInternal.ts` — `useSpreadsheetImportInternal` (context reader).\n- `hooks/useOpenSpreadsheetImportDialog.ts` — `useOpenSpreadsheetImportDialog` (opens modal + sets options state).\n- `states/spreadsheetImportDialogState.ts` — `spreadsheetImportDialogState` (Jotai atom: `{ isOpen, isStepBarVisible, options }`).\n- `states/spreadsheetImportCreatedRecordsProgressState.ts` — `spreadsheetImportCreatedRecordsProgressState`.\n- `constants/SpreadsheetImportModalId.ts` — `SPREADSHEET_IMPORT_MODAL_ID`.\n\nWizard flow (`steps/`):\n- `steps/types/SpreadsheetImportStep.ts`, `SpreadsheetImportStepType.ts` — step union: `upload | selectSheet | selectHeader | matchColumns | validateData | importData | loading`.\n- `steps/components/SpreadsheetImportStepper.tsx` — `SpreadsheetImportStepper` (switch over step state, error snackbars).\n- `steps/components/SpreadsheetImportStepperContainer.tsx` — header + `StepBar` (Upload File / Match Columns / Validate Data).\n- `steps/components/UploadStep/UploadStep.tsx` + `components/DropZone.tsx` — file drop, max-records check, workbook → rows, auto-match columns.\n- `steps/components/SelectSheetStep/SelectSheetStep.tsx`, `SelectHeaderStep/SelectHeaderStep.tsx` (+ `SelectHeaderTable`, `SelectColumn`).\n- `steps/components/MatchColumnsStep/MatchColumnsStep.tsx` + `components/` — column↔field mapping UI, sub-field/select matching (`ColumnGrid`, `UnmatchColumnBanner`, `SubMatchingSelect*`, `UserTableColumn`, `TemplateColumn`), states under `MatchColumnsStep/components/states/` (`initialComputedColumnsState` → `initialComputedColumnsSelector`, `matchColumnsState`; `suggestedFieldsByColumnHeaderState`).\n- `steps/components/ValidationStep/ValidationStep.tsx` — **per-row error feedback**: grid with error rows, \"Show only rows with errors\" toggle, row deletion, \"Finish flow with errors\" dialog; computes `SpreadsheetImportImportValidationResult`.\n- `steps/components/ValidationStep/types.ts` — `ImportedStructuredRowMetadata`, `Error`, `Errors`.\n- `steps/components/ImportDataStep.tsx` — progress screen (\"X out of Y records imported\").\n- `steps/components/ValidationStep/components/columns.tsx` — `generateColumns` (editable cells, error/warning highlighting).\n- `components/SpreadsheetImportTable.tsx` — `react-data-grid` wrapper with error/warning/info cell colors.\n\nHooks:\n- `hooks/useComputeColumnSuggestionsAndAutoMatch.ts` — `useComputeColumnSuggestionsAndAutoMatch` (uses Fuse.js auto-matching).\n- `hooks/useSpreadsheetImportInitialStep.ts`, `hooks/useHideStepBar.ts`.\n\nCSV/XLSX parsing:\n- `utils/readFilesAsync.ts` — `readFileAsync` (FileReader → ArrayBuffer).\n- `utils/mapWorkbook.ts` — `mapWorkbook` (uses `xlsx-ugnis` `sheet_to_json`, cleans ZWJ protection).\n- `utils/exceedsMaxRecords.ts` — `exceedsMaxRecords`.\n- `constants/SpreadsheetMaxRecordImportCapacity.ts` — `SPREADSHEET_MAX_RECORD_IMPORT_CAPACITY = 10000`.\n- `constants/SpreadsheetImportCreateRecordsBatchSize.ts` — `SPREADSHEET_IMPORT_CREATE_RECORDS_BATCH_SIZE = 200`.\n\nValidation / normalization:\n- `utils/dataMutations.ts` — `addErrorsAndRunHooks`: runs `tableHook`, `rowHook`, then field `fieldValidationDefinitions` (`unique`, `required`, `regex`, `function`), attaches `__errors` per row.\n- `utils/normalizeTableData.ts` — `normalizeTableData` (checkbox/select/multiSelect/ignored column mapping).\n- `utils/normalizeCheckboxValue.ts`, `utils/spreadsheetImportParseMultiSelectOptionsOrThrow.ts`, `utils/getMatchedColumnsWithFuse.ts`, `utils/setColumn.ts`, `utils/setIgnoreColumn.ts`, `utils/setSubColumn.ts`, `utils/uniqueEntries.ts`, `utils/findUnmatchedRequiredFields.ts`, `utils/getFieldOptions.ts`, `utils/spreadsheetImportBuildFieldOptions.ts`, `utils/spreadsheetImportGetSubFieldOptions.ts`, `utils/getShortNestedFieldLabel.ts`, `utils/spreadsheetImportHasNestedFields.ts`.\n\nCSV safety (export round-trip protection):\n- `constants/CsvDangerousCharacters.ts` — `CSV_DANGEROUS_CHARACTERS = /^[=+\\-@\\t\\r]/`.\n- `constants/CsvInjectionPreventionZwj.ts` — `CSV_INJECTION_PREVENTION_ZWJ = '\\u200D'`.\n- `utils/sanitizeValueForCSVExport.ts` — `sanitizeValueForCSVExport`.\n- `utils/formatValueForCSV.ts` — `formatValueForCSV` (quote/escape; NOT security).\n- `utils/cleanZWJFromImportedValue.ts`, `utils/containsCSVProtectionZWJ.ts`.\n\nRow / field / error types (`types/`):\n- `SpreadsheetImportImportedRow.ts` → `ImportedRow = Array<string | undefined>`.\n- `SpreadsheetImportImportedStructuredRow.ts` → `ImportedStructuredRow = { [key: string]: string | boolean | undefined }`.\n- `SpreadsheetImportImportValidationResult.ts` → `{ validStructuredRows, invalidStructuredRows, allStructuredRows }`.\n- `SpreadsheetImportInfo.ts` → `{ message, level }`; `SpreadsheetImportErrorLevel.ts` → `'info' | 'warning' | 'error'`.\n- `SpreadsheetImportField.ts`, `SpreadsheetImportFields.ts`, `SpreadsheetImportFieldType.ts` (`checkbox|select|multiSelect|input`), `SpreadsheetImportFieldValidationDefinition.ts` (`required|unique|regex|function|object`), `SpreadsheetImportFieldOption.ts`, `SpreadsheetImportDialogOptions.ts`, `SpreadsheetImportRowHook.ts`, `SpreadsheetImportTableHook.ts`, `SpreadsheetColumn.ts`, `SpreadsheetColumns.ts`, `SpreadsheetColumnType.ts`, `SpreadsheetMatchedOptions.ts`, `SpreadsheetImportTableHook.ts`, `index.ts` (barrel).\n\n### B. Object-record integration — `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/spreadsheet-import/`\n- `hooks/useOpenObjectRecordsSpreadsheetImportDialog.ts` — `useOpenObjectRecordsSpreadsheetImportDialog(objectNameSingular)`: filters importable fields, builds import fields, and on submit converts valid rows and calls **`batchCreateManyRecords({ recordsToCreate, upsert: true })`**; evicts Apollo cache; error snackbar.\n- `hooks/useBuildSpreadSheetImportFields.ts` — `useBuildSpreadSheetImportFields` → `buildSpreadsheetImportFields`: maps field metadata types to `SpreadsheetImportField`; composite sub-fields; MANY_TO_ONE relation connect via target object's unique-constraint fields; select/multiSelect options; **filters out `ACTOR`**.\n- `utils/buildRecordFromImportedStructuredRow.ts` — `buildRecordFromImportedStructuredRow`: converts `ImportedStructuredRow` → GraphQL input (currency micros, address, links, phones via libphonenumber, emails, full name, rich text, relation `connect`, arrays/multi-select JSON, RAW_JSON, dates).\n- `utils/getSpreadSheetFieldValidationDefinitions.ts` — `getSpreadSheetFieldValidationDefinitions`: per-type `rule: 'function'` validators (number, UUID, email, URL, phone, date, JSON, rating, array).\n- `utils/spreadsheetImportGetUnicityTableHook.ts` — `spreadsheetImportGetUnicityTableHook`: **duplicate detection within the imported file** (not against DB) for unique indexes (id, composite indexes, multi-field).\n- `utils/spreadsheetImportFilterAvailableFieldMetadataItems.ts` — `spreadsheetImportFilterAvailableFieldMetadataItems`: keeps active, non-hidden-system (plus `id`), excludes `deletedAt`; **RELATION kept only if `relation?.type === MANY_TO_ONE`**; ACTOR excluded.\n- `utils/getLinksVariant.ts`, `utils/spreadSheetGetRelationConnectSubFieldKey.ts`, `utils/spreadsheetImportGetRelationConnectSubFieldLabel.ts`, `utils/spreadsheetImportGetCompositeSubFieldKey.ts`, `utils/spreadsheetImportGetCompositeSubFieldLabelWithFieldLabel.ts`.\n\nUI entry point:\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu-item/engine-command/record/no-selection/components/ImportRecordsNoSelectionRecordCommand.tsx` — `ImportRecordsNoSelectionRecordCommand`: closes side panel, calls `openObjectRecordsSpreadsheetImportDialog()`.\n- Mounted in `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-index/components/RecordIndexViewBar.tsx` via `<SpreadsheetImportProvider>`.\n- Wired through `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu-item/engine-command/constants/EngineComponentKeyHeadlessComponentMap.tsx` under `EngineComponentKey.IMPORT_RECORDS`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Backend import\n\n**None exists in this checkout.** Confirmed absent:\n- No `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/import*` or `engine/**/import*` record-import module.\n- No `ImportJob` / `ImportJobItem` entity, no `import-job` queue/worker.\n- No `uploadImportFile` / `importRecords` GraphQL mutation (checked `packages/twenty-front/src/generated/graphql.ts`, `.../generated-metadata/graphql.ts`, and `packages/twenty-client-sdk/src/metadata/generated/schema.graphql`).\n\nWhat backend *does* support the flow:\n- Standard object-record `createMany` mutation (with `upsert`) — runner under `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/api/graphql/graphql-query-runner/` and `workspace-resolver-builder/` (`resolver-method-names.ts`, `workspace-resolver.factory.ts`). Frontend caller: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/hooks/useBatchCreateManyRecords.ts` → `useCreateManyRecords.ts` (`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/hooks/useCreateManyRecordsMutation.ts`).\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/record-crud/` — generic record CRUD types (`create-many-records-params.type.ts`, etc.) used by tools/API, not CSV-specific.\n\nGating / metadata that reference import:\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/permission-flag/constants/standard-permission-flag-definitions.constant.ts` — `PermissionFlagType.IMPORT_CSV` (lines ~137), `EXPORT_CSV` (~142).\n- `packages/twenty-shared/src/constants/PermissionFlagType.ts` (`IMPORT_CSV`, `EXPORT_CSV`), `.../SystemPermissionFlag.ts` (universal IDs).\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/constants/standard-command-menu-item.constant.ts` — `importRecords` (line 261, availability `pageType == \"INDEX_PAGE\" and not hasAnySoftDeleteFilterOnView and permissionFlags.IMPORT_CSV`), `exportRecords` (196), `exportView` (283), `exportNoteToPdf` (177).\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/command-menu-item/enums/engine-component-key.enum.ts` — `IMPORT_RECORDS`, `EXPORT_RECORDS`, `EXPORT_VIEW`, `EXPORT_NOTE_TO_PDF`.\n\nUnrelated import modules (do not confuse): calendar-event/messaging message-import managers, onboarding-recent-messages-import, and `packages/twenty-apps/public/call-recorder/src/logic-functions/flows/handle-call-recording-artifacts-import-job.util.ts` (app-level, not native).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Export\n\nEntirely frontend, browser-side CSV:\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-index/export/hooks/useRecordIndexExportRecords.ts` — exports `generateCsv` (uses `json-2-csv`; adds `Id` column; drops non-MANY_TO_ONE relations; flattens composite fields; sanitizes strings via `sanitizeValueForCSVExport`; `excelBOM: true`), `displayedExportProgress`, `csvDownloader` (Blob + `file-saver` `saveAs`), and `useRecordIndexExportRecords`.\n- `.../export/hooks/useRecordIndexLazyFetchRecords.ts` — paginated record fetch + progress callback (backs export).\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-show/hooks/useExportSingleRecord.ts` — `useExportSingleRecord` (single record via `useFindOneRecord`).\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/object-options-dropdown/hooks/useExportProcessRecordsForCSV.ts` — `useExportProcessRecordsForCSV` (currency micros → amount; JSON-stringifies multi-select/array/raw-json/files).\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/object-options-dropdown/constants/ExportTableDataDefaultPageSize.ts`.\n- UI: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu-item/engine-command/record/components/ExportRecordsCommand.tsx` — `ExportRecordsCommand` (handles both `EXPORT_RECORDS` selection export and `EXPORT_VIEW`; filename `${nameSingular}.csv`; per-command progress). `ExportNoteSingleRecordCommand.tsx` handles `EXPORT_NOTE_TO_PDF` (note/task).\n- CSV safety utilities shared with import: `sanitizeValueForCSVExport`, `formatValueForCSV`, `CSV_INJECTION_PREVENTION_ZWJ`, `cleanZWJFromImportedValue`.\n\nNo frontend/backed export GraphQL mutation exists. Server-side adjacent exports only:\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/database/commands/workspace-export/` — `WorkspaceExportService.exportWorkspace` + `WorkspaceExportCommand` (CLI: workspace → SQL INSERT/COPY file), with utils (`generate-workspace-schema-ddl.util.ts`, `format-sql-value.util.ts`, etc.).\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/application/application-manifest/services/application-manifest-export.service.ts` and `.../application-development/dtos/export-application.input.ts` + GraphQL `exportApplication` (`ApplicationExport`) — app manifest export, unrelated to records.\n\n---\n\n## 4. How `task` is treated by import\n\nThere is **no task-specific code path** in the importer. Tasks go through the same generic pipeline as any object.\n\nTask standard fields — `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/utils/field-metadata/compute-task-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts`:\n- `title` TEXT — **`isNullable: true`** (not required).\n- `bodyV2` RICH_TEXT, `dueAt` DATE_TIME, `status` SELECT (`TODO` default; options TODO / IN_PROGRESS / DONE), `position` POSITION, `createdBy`/`updatedBy` ACTOR, `searchVector` TS_VECTOR.\n- `assignee` RELATION **MANY_TO_ONE** → `workspaceMember` (`assignedTasks`), nullable, `onDelete: SET_NULL`, join `assigneeId`.\n- `taskTargets` RELATION **ONE_TO_MANY** → `taskTarget` (join object; the polymorphic person/company/opportunity link via `compute-task-target-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts`).\n- `attachments` / `timelineActivities` ONE_TO_MANY side effects.\n\nConsequences in the importer:\n- **Required fields:** none of task's own fields are required by validation (no `required` rules generated); the object-record API may still reject on non-null constraints. `getSpreadSheetFieldValidationDefinitions` only adds type/format checks.\n- **Relation handling:** only MANY_TO_ONE relations are importable (`spreadsheetImportFilterAvailableFieldMetadataItems`, `handleRelationField`). So `assignee` **is** importable via relation-connect using the target's unique-constraint fields (`getUniqueConstraintsFields` always includes `id`, plus `workspaceMember.userEmail` which is `isUnique: true` — see `compute-workspace-member-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts` line ~330).\n- **`taskTargets` (the task↔person/company/opportunity many-to-many via `taskTarget`) is NOT importable** — it is ONE_TO_MANY and is filtered out. There is no many-to-many / nested create handling in `buildRecordFromImportedStructuredRow`, which only emits `{ connect: { where: ... } }` for MANY_TO_ONE.\n- **Excluded field types overall:** ACTOR, FILES, POSITION, MORPH_RELATION, TS_VECTOR (`useBuildSpreadSheetImportFields`).\n- **Permission checks:** the command menu item is gated by `permissionFlags.IMPORT_CSV` and `pageType == \"INDEX_PAGE\"` + no soft-delete filter (server constant, see §2); actual writes are governed by standard object permissions on the `createMany` mutation. No per-row permission checks in the importer.\n- **Upsert semantics:** submit uses `batchCreateManyRecords({ upsert: true })`, so imported rows with IDs/unique keys update existing records.\n- **Row errors:** validation/unicity errors are shown per row in `ValidationStep`; invalid rows are silently dropped (with a confirmation dialog) — only `validStructuredRows` are submitted. There is no per-row backend error storage; any `createMany` failure is surfaced as a single error snackbar.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Existing tests (import validation / escaping / error feedback)\n\nGeneric engine (`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/spreadsheet-import/utils/__tests__/`):\n- `csvSecurity.test.ts` — `CSV_DANGEROUS_CHARACTERS` regex, `sanitizeValueForCSVExport`, `cleanZWJFromImportedValue`, `containsCSVProtectionZWJ`, export→import round-trip, international characters.\n- `formatValueForCSV.test.ts` — commas/quotes/newlines/JSON/null formatting.\n- `dataMutations.test.ts` — `addErrorsAndRunHooks`: rowHook/tableHook, required/regex/unique/function validation, empty-value handling.\n- `normalizeTableData.test.ts` — checkbox/booleanMatches, select/multiSelect mapping, ignored columns.\n- `normalizeCheckboxValue.test.ts`, `spreadsheetImportParseMultiSelectOptionsOrThrow.test.ts`, `mapWorkbook.test.ts`, `readFilesAsync.test.ts`, `exceedsMaxRecords.test.ts`, `uniqueEntries.test.ts`, `setColumn.test.ts`, `setIgnoreColumn.test.ts`, `setSubColumn.test.ts`, `getFieldOptions.test.ts`, `getShortNestedFieldLabel.test.ts`, `findUnmatchedRequiredFields.test.ts`.\n\nEngine hooks:\n- `hooks/__tests__/useSpreadsheetImport.test.tsx` (dialog open/options state), `useSpreadsheetImportInternal.test.tsx`, `useSpreadsheetImportInitialStep.test.ts`.\n\nObject-record integration (`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/spreadsheet-import/...`):\n- `utils/__tests__/buildRecordFromImportedStructuredRow.test.ts` — full row→input conversion, phone without calling code, relation composite sub-fields, lowercase relation email, links normalization, empty row.\n- `utils/__tests__/spreadsheetImportGetUnicityTableHook.test.ts` — duplicate detection on composite field / id / multi-field indexes.\n- `hooks/__tests__/useOpenObjectRecordsSpreadsheetImportDialog.test.ts` — dialog config and `batchCreateManyRecords` invocation.\n- `hooks/__tests__/useBuildSpreadSheetImportFields.test.tsx` — field building (basic/select/composite/ACTOR filtering/unsupported/relation).\n\nExport:\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-index/export/hooks/__tests__/useRecordIndexExportRecords.test.ts` — `generateCsv` formatting, multi-select/array JSON, CSV-injection ZWJ prevention (all 6 dangerous chars), UTF-8 BOM bytes, international chars, `displayedExportProgress`.\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/object-options-dropdown/hooks/__tests__/useExportProcessRecordsForCSV.test.ts`.\n\nNo e2e tests for import/export (`packages/twenty-e2e-testing` has none).\n\n---\n\n## 6. App SDK capabilities related to import/export\n\n### Does the SDK expose import?\n**No.** `packages/twenty-sdk` has no CSV/import/export API:\n- `twenty-sdk/front-component` barrel (`src/sdk/front-component/index.ts`) exposes only: `uploadFile`, `navigate`, `openSidePanelPage`, `closeSidePanel`, `copyToClipboard`, `enqueueSnackbar`, `openCommandConfirmationModal`, `updateProgress`, `unmountFrontComponent`, `getApplicationVariable`, `Trans`, hooks (`useRecordId`, `useSelectedRecordIds`, `useUserId`, `useLocale`, `useColorScheme`, `useFrontComponentId`, `useFrontComponentExecutionContext`, `useTimelineActivityId`, `useTranslate`), and `Command`/`CommandLink`/`CommandModal`/`CommandOpenSidePanelPage`. There is **no spreadsheet-import host function or modal API** (`globals/frontComponentHostCommunicationApi.ts` defines the host contract; no import entry).\n- `twenty-sdk/logic-function` (`src/sdk/logic-function/index.ts`) exposes connections, KV, jobs, timeline, `runAgent`, `getConnection` — no import.\n- `twenty-client-sdk` (`src/core`, `src/metadata`, `src/rest`) exposes generated Core/Metadata clients and a REST client — no import/export operations.\n\n### Can an app front-component reuse the native import UI/store?\n**Not directly.** The `spreadsheetImportDialogState` atom and `useOpenObjectRecordsSpreadsheetImportDialog` are internal to `twenty-front` and are not re-exported to apps. Front components run sandboxed and only get the host functions above; there is no host bridge for opening the native import modal or reading its store.\n\nWhat an app *can* do:\n- Define its own `commandMenuItem` that opens its own front component: `defineCommandMenuItem` requires `frontComponentUniversalIdentifier` (`packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/command-menu-items/`). The in-repo example is `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/command-menu-items/create-document.command-menu-item.ts` + `front-components/create-document-command.front-component.tsx`. Apps **cannot** set a native `EngineComponentKey.IMPORT_RECORDS` — the SDK only allows a front-component target, so they cannot trigger the native import command.\n- Build their own importer in a front component (e.g. parse CSV with a bundled lib, then call the app's own logic function / API). `uploadFile` is available for file upload plumbing, but no native CSV parse/validate/mapping helpers are exported.\n- Grant the native commands to roles via `PermissionFlag` (`packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/roles/permission-flag-type.ts` re-exports `PermissionFlagType`, including `IMPORT_CSV` / `EXPORT_CSV` from `twenty-shared/constants`). This makes the native Import/Export buttons appear for users with that role, but does not expose programmatic import to apps.\n\n### `internal/real-estate`\nNo import/export capabilities: it has only `objects/`, `fields/`, `views/`, `roles/`, `page-layouts/`, `navigation-menu-items/`, `logic-functions/post-install.ts`, and `application.config.ts`. There are no `front-components/` and no CSV/import logic (the grep hits were only `import` statements).\n\nThe richer reference for app front-component + command-menu patterns is `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents` (front components, command menu items, logic functions), not `real-estate`.\n\n---\n\n## Practical implication\n\nIf you want task bulk-import behavior beyond what the generic client-side importer offers (e.g. many-to-many `taskTargets`, per-row backend errors, large-file server parsing), **you would be building it from scratch** — there is no native server import job to extend. The existing extension seam is `useOpenObjectRecordsSpreadsheetImportDialog` + `buildRecordFromImportedStructuredRow` (frontend) and the standard `createMany` resolver (backend).\n</task_result>\n</task>"
